# Elastic Beanstalk deploy bundle — what `eb deploy` ships to
# Jackpotsworld-env (see .elasticbeanstalk/config.yml).
#
# Why this file has to exist at all: with no .ebignore, the EB CLI falls
# back to `git archive`, and this app is a *subdirectory* of its git repo.
# That produces two problems at once — the archive is rooted at the repo
# root, so manage.py/Procfile don't land at the top level where EB expects
# them, and the bundle sweeps in everything else tracked in the repo,
# including two committed virtualenvs (~460 MB) and the frontend source.
# That tips it past EB's hard 512 MB archive limit and the deploy fails
# outright with FileTooLargeError.
#
# Presence of this file switches the EB CLI to zipping *this* directory
# instead, which fixes the layout, and the exclusions below keep the
# bundle small.
#
# Every path listed here is untracked in git, so excluding it ships exactly
# what the previous git-archive deploys shipped. In particular media/ was
# never part of the bundle, so nothing here removes live uploads.

# Local virtualenv — EB builds its own from requirements.txt.
venv/
# The *other* virtualenv. Two exist in this checkout and only one was
# listed, so ~91 MB of compressed site-packages shipped on every single
# deploy - the largest thing in the bundle, and pure waste: EB installs
# from requirements.txt on the instance and never looks at this.
.venv/
# Call recordings. VOICE_CALL_RECORDING_ROOT defaults to a sibling of
# MEDIA_ROOT, which locally resolves inside this directory - so recorded
# customer audio was being swept into the deploy archive and shipped to
# the instance. Runtime data never belongs in a code bundle, least of all
# this kind.
call-recordings/

# User uploads (663 MB) and runtime logs. Never belonged in a deploy
# artifact; EB replaces /var/app/current wholesale on every deploy.
media/
logs/

# Regenerated on each instance by the 04_collectstatic container_command
# in .ebextensions/01_django.config.
staticfiles/

# Local-only settings. EB supplies configuration through environment
# variables (`eb printenv`), and shipping local DB credentials to
# production is exactly the kind of thing that should never be possible.
.env
.env.local

# Local sqlite scratch DBs — production runs MySQL on RDS.
db.sqlite3
*.sqlite3

# EB CLI's own workspace, including its cache of previous application
# version zips (currently ~1.4 GB). The CLI excludes this itself; listed
# for the benefit of anyone reading the bundle contents.
.elasticbeanstalk/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
